// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`contextImport.v2 prompt (F-9.11) > matches the golden messages for the fixture and asks for the feature output budget 1`] = `
[
  {
    "content": "You are the context-library feature inside a novel-writing app, sorting the author’s own notes into their story bible. Read the document and list every person, place, and thing it describes under the category it belongs to. Use only what the document states, in the author’s words; never invent or embellish. When someone or something is one of the existing sheets listed (or a nickname of one), use that sheet’s name and category exactly and put the other names in "aliases". Categories as kind (what goes in it): field ids — character (people and beings with a name): age, born, gender, appearance, personality, background, goals, relationships; setting (places: cities, rooms, regions, worlds): type, description, atmosphere, features, associatedCharacters; world (anything about the world no other category fits): category, description, rules, impact; magic (magic, powers, and how they work): description, source, rules, costs, practitioners, impact; faction (groups, orders, guilds, houses, governments, armies): type, description, goals, leadership, members, relationships; religion (faiths, gods, cults, and their practices): description, deities, beliefs, practices, followers; creature (animals, monsters, and species): description, appearance, habitat, behavior, abilities; item (objects, weapons, relics, and artifacts): description, appearance, origin, powers, owner; culture (peoples, nations, customs, and ways of life): description, homeland, customs, values; history (wars, eras, and past events): when, description, causes, consequences, associatedCharacters; language (languages, scripts, and dialects): description, speakers, sound, examples; technology (machines, inventions, and how they work): description, howItWorks, limits, impact; lore (myths, prophecies, and stories told in the world): description, origin, truth. Use world only when no other category fits. When several things share a kind no category fits, you may propose a new category in "categories" with a short kind, a plural name, a singular, and up to 6 field names, and use that kind and those field names for them. Put a fact in a field when one fits; keep one-line fields (age, born, gender, type, category, owner, when) short. Everything else about it goes in "details" as short paragraphs, each starting with a topic and a colon ("History: …"). What fits no sheet (themes, the plot outline, rules for the book) goes in "notes" the same way. When an image file name or the text says whom or what a listed image shows, add it to "images". Reply with JSON only: {"entities":[{"kind":"character","name":"Mara Vell","aliases":["Mara"],"fields":{"age":"34"},"details":["History: …"]},{"kind":"ships","name":"The Gull","fields":{"Crew":"twelve"}}],"categories":[{"kind":"ships","name":"Ships","noun":"ship","fields":["Crew","Home port"]}],"notes":["Theme: …"],"images":[{"file":"mara.png","name":"Mara Vell"}]}. Empty lists are fine.",
    "role": "system",
  },
  {
    "content": "The project's own categories:
c-ships (Ships): crew, homePort

Existing sheets by kind:
character: Mara Vell, Tomas
magic: The Weave

Images: mara-portrait.png

Document "notes.md":
The Weave costs a memory per knot.

The Gull: a cutter, crew of twelve.",
    "role": "user",
  },
]
